[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: User Requirements
UID: YAAP-UR
DATE: @GIT_COMMIT_DATETIME
PREFIX: UR-

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Introduction

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the user requirements for Yet Another Audio Player (Yaap),
a time accurate desktop audio player.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Supported Audio Playback

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-001
TITLE: Supported Audio Formats
STATEMENT: The user shall be able to play audio tracks in supported audio formats.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-002
TITLE: Unsupported Audio Formats
STATEMENT: The user shall be able to identify audio files that Yaap cannot play.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-001

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Playing files

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-003
TITLE: Playing local files
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to play supported audio files stored on their device.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-004
TITLE: Cloud storage Connections
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to connect Yaap to supported cloud storage providers.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-005
TITLE: Playing Remote files
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to play supported audio files stored with a connected cloud
provider.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-006
TITLE: Audio Quality
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to play supported audio tracks at the quality provided 
by the source audio.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback Position

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-007
TITLE: View Playback Position
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to view the current playback position of an audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-008
TITLE: Elapsed Playback Time
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to determine the elapsed playback time of an audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-009
TITLE: Seek Playback Position
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to seek to a requested position within an audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-010
TITLE: Remaining Playback Time
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to determine the remaining playback time of an audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-011
TITLE: Playback Information
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to access and receive playback through the operating 
system's supported media-control interface, where available.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-005

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback Customization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-012
TITLE: Playback Speed
STATEMENT: The user shall be able to adjust the playback speed of an audio track.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-013
TITLE: Playback Pitch
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to adjust the playback pitch of an audio track independently 
of playback speed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-014
TITLE: Playback Volume
STATEMENT: The user shall be able to adjust the playback volume of an audio track.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-015
TITLE: Audio Processing Configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to configure the available audio processing options.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: UR-016
TITLE: Active Playback Customisations
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall be able to determine which playback customizations are 
currently active.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: BR-006

